    "theme": {
      "_comment": "Sub-topic of the keyword, used to split one big topic (a single occasion export) into pillars and to merge question variants into one post. Checked in this order: the first 'patterns' match wins; 'weak_patterns' are only tried when no theme matched strongly. 'generic' words are ignored when deciding whether two keywords ask the same thing ('when is thanksgiving' = 'what day is thanksgiving'). 'need' is the reader need used when the reader-need rules find nothing. year_only: theme for an occasion keyword that only adds a year ('thanksgiving 2026'). 'fallback': when topic-map splits a big pillar by theme and this theme is too small to be a pillar of its own, its posts join the fallback theme's pillar.",
